      "normalized_sha256": "e28394b585c4090679938a1fc2a49542a90c06f9fd53d8d2ea93cb550aecd2b6",
      "rationale": "This rule is the expansion of the INTERSPERSE-BODY syntax macro into the exact statement-list proof term; it names program syntax and is expanded before runtime execution rather than adding an operational or mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-e28394b585c4090679938a1fc2a49542a90c06f9fd53d8d2ea93cb550aecd2b6",
      "start_line": 8,
      "text": "  rule INTERSPERSE-BODY\n    => If(Name(\"result\"),\n          Expr(Call(Attribute(Name(\"result\"), \"append\"),\n                    Name(\"delimeter\"))) .Stmts,\n          .Stmts)\n       Expr(Call(Attribute(Name(\"result\"), \"append\"), Name(\"number\")))\n       .Stmts"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "671fd3686197e0c91cef745f9b7af75d1bd0f7277cabab95a54dc8fbf6e1ef79",
      "rationale": "This is the base equation of the total intersperseAcc mathematical summary: when no input remains, the accumulated output is the defined result.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-671fd3686197e0c91cef745f9b7af75d1bd0f7277cabab95a54dc8fbf6e1ef79",
      "start_line": 20,
      "text": "  rule intersperseAcc(ACC:ValSeq, .ValSeq, _:Val) => ACC"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 23,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "386331eb5a2c59cc86798243ff1afd3badb062dc83a886655fce827ef4f75b24",
      "rationale": "This is the recursive defining equation for intersperseAcc with an empty accumulator and nonempty remaining input; it consumes the first input without introducing a delimiter.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-386331eb5a2c59cc86798243ff1afd3badb062dc83a886655fce827ef4f75b24",
      "start_line": 22,
      "text": "  rule intersperseAcc(.ValSeq, vCons(X:Val, REST:ValSeq), D:Val)\n    => intersperseAcc(vCons(X, .ValSeq), REST, D)"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 32,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "b0a9306232910cc5bd1efab08c4f20853e642eec8176e7d9e7d39d1d46f375cd",
      "rationale": "This is the recursive defining equation for intersperseAcc with a nonempty accumulator and nonempty remaining input; it defines the next accumulator by appending the delimiter and next value while structurally decreasing REST.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-b0a9306232910cc5bd1efab08c4f20853e642eec8176e7d9e7d39d1d46f375cd",
      "start_line": 25,
      "text": "  rule intersperseAcc(vCons(A:Val, AS:ValSeq),\n                      vCons(X:Val, REST:ValSeq), D:Val)\n    => intersperseAcc(\n         valSeqConcat(\n           valSeqConcat(vCons(A, AS), vCons(D, .ValSeq)),\n           vCons(X, .ValSeq)),\n         REST,\n         D)"
    }
  ],
